From: SuperLeiyan <5438286+SuperLeiyan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:26:56 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] PC5: the touchpad press is the Xbox controller's Back

In Xbox controller mode, Back (View) was the Create button only. The
console answers Create with its own share menu, so a game whose menu or
map is on Back brought that up as well. The touchpad press, which was
Guide (a button games read only through XInput's hidden ordinal), is now
Back too; Create stays Back for the games and players that use it.
---
 docs/WINE_PS5_BUILD.md       | 2 +-
 native/pw_wine_display.c     | 4 +++-
 native/pw_wine_display.h     | 2 +-
 tests/test_pw_wine_display.c | 2 +-
 4 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/WINE_PS5_BUILD.md b/docs/WINE_PS5_BUILD.md
index 1a50af3..d959433 100644
--- a/docs/WINE_PS5_BUILD.md
+++ b/docs/WINE_PS5_BUILD.md
@@ -1176,7 +1176,7 @@ The title runs one game per process (`src/pw_wine_launch.h`):
     0 (see [XInput controller](#xinput-controller)).
     - Cross, Circle, Square and Triangle are A, B, X and Y. L1/R1 are the
       shoulders, L2/R2 the analog triggers and L3/R3 the stick clicks.
-      Options is Start, Create is Back and the touchpad is Guide.
+      Options is Start; the touchpad and Create are Back (Create also opens the console's share menu).
     - The sticks are scaled to XInput's range, with y up.
     - The rumble a game asks for runs the DualSense's motors through
       `scePadSetVibration`: XInput's left motor is the large one. The
diff --git a/native/pw_wine_display.c b/native/pw_wine_display.c
